13. FIVE CORE GAMES

Develop five distinct genres:

GAME 1 — UNIT CIRCLE QUEST
An exploration game covering angles, radians, quadrants, trigonometric ratios, identities, graphs and equations.

GAME 2 — PROJECTILE LAB: MISSION CONTROL
A physics puzzle game covering vectors, motion equations, launch conditions and the limitations of idealised models.

GAME 3 — ALGEBRA ARENA
A turn-based mathematical strategy game using valid algebraic transformations, equations, complex numbers, sequences and combinatorics.

GAME 4 — FORCE & MOTION BUILDER
A simulation-based construction game involving forces, friction, equilibrium, energy and mechanical systems.

GAME 5 — GRAPH ESCAPE
A visual puzzle game involving coordinate geometry, straight lines, conic sections, functions and introductory calculus intuition.

Every game must include:

