22. AUTHENTICATION AND CHILD SAFETY

Provide guest access.

For optional accounts, implement email/password authentication, email verification, secure password reset, rate limiting and breach-password protections.

Use an established identity system where appropriate rather than inventing password security.

Store passwords only as appropriately salted, computationally expensive password hashes on the server. Never log passwords or reset tokens.

Evaluate Google sign-in and passkeys as optional additions.

Implement account export and deletion flows.

Use privacy by default, minimal collection, short and justified retention, private progress and explicit consent where required.

Have qualified legal counsel review applicable Indian data-protection requirements, GDPR children's-data rules where relevant, COPPA where applicable and distribution-platform policies.

Do not claim legal compliance without an appropriate review.

